{
  "version": 1,
  "description": "Pay periods. input: { anchor: date, now: local date-time }. Periods are 14 days long and sit on a grid of 14-day steps from the anchor, forwards and backwards (the anchor may be in the future). Early start: 'now' is shifted forward 9 hours before its date is taken, so from 15:00:00 on the day before a period starts, that period is already the current one. expected: { periods: [3 items] } in the order 'This Pay Period' (the period containing the shifted date), 'Next Pay Period', 'Following Period'. Each item: { label, key (= start), start, end (= start + 13 days, inclusive), payday (= start), isCurrent (true only for the first) }, dates as YYYY-MM-DD. The reference always applies the 3 PM shift; it does not read the stored EarlyStart setting (see README.md).",
